     vviioommbb — VirtIO memory ballooning driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     vviioommbb**  aatt vviirrttiioo??

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vviioommbb driver supports the virtio-compliant memory ballooning device.

     Memory ballooning works as follows:

     1.   The host operator requests a guest to return some amount of memory
          to the host (via, for example, the QEMU monitor balloon command).
     2.   The hypervisor sends the request via the VirtIO memory ballooning
          device.
     3.   The guest vviioommbb driver requests allocation of that amount of physi‐
          cal memory from the OpenBSD memory management system.
     4.   The vviioommbb device tells the hypervisor the guest physical memory ad‐
          dress of the allocated memory via the VirtIO memory ballooning de‐
          vice.

